Interface- implemnts. Solves the issue of multiple inheritance. 

interface Flyable{
    void fly();    
}

class Bird implements Flyable{
    public void fly(){
    System.out.println("Bird is flying");
}
}
public class Main
{
	public static void main(String[] args) {
		 Bird b = new Bird();
		 b.fly();
	}
}



A class can implement MULTIPLE interfaces. This is the way of showing multiple interface. 
interface Eat {
    void eat();
}

interface Sleep {
    void sleep();
}

class Human implements Eat, Sleep {

    @Override
    public void eat() {
        System.out.println("Human eats");
    }

    @Override
    public void sleep() {
        System.out.println("Human sleeps");
    }
}

public class Main {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Human h = new Human();

        h.sleep();
        h.eat();
    }
}

